    "items": [
      {
        "id": "def-score-and-fisher-information",
        "kind": "definition",
        "title": "Score and Fisher information",
        "statement": "For a dominated parametric model with selected differentiable density representatives, define the score as the derivative of the log density on the positive-density support. For d=1 define scalar Fisher information by the expected squared score; for d>1, when the vector score is square-integrable, define the information matrix by the expected score outer product. The definition adds no parameter measurability or common-support hypothesis.",
