        "id": "thm-score-mean-zero-and-information-identity",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "title": "Mean-zero score and the information identity",
        "statement": "On an open parameter set, suppose a selected density family has a fixed positive support on a neighborhood, is twice continuously differentiable there, and its first and second parameter derivatives have local integrable envelopes. If the score has finite second moment, then its expectation is zero and the Fisher information matrix equals the negative expected log-likelihood Hessian. This is a sufficient regularity setup, not a necessary characterization.",
