        "id": "thm-cramer-rao-lower-bound",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "title": "Scalar Cramér–Rao lower bound",
        "statement": "For a scalar parameter in an open interval, let T have finite variance and mean ψ(θ) locally, let the score have mean zero and finite positive information I(θ), and assume Covθ(T,Sθ)=ψ′(θ). Then Varθ(T)≥ψ′(θ)²/I(θ), with equality exactly when T−ψ(θ)=(ψ′(θ)/I(θ))Sθ almost surely. Common support and an integrable derivative envelope are one sufficient route to the score and covariance identities, not necessary hypotheses for every valid bound.",
