      {
        "id": "thm-multivariate-cramer-rao-bound",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "title": "Multivariate Cramér–Rao bound",
        "statement": "For an open d-dimensional parameter set, let T be a k-vector estimator unbiased coordinatewise with finite covariance, let the score have mean zero and finite nonsingular information matrix I(θ), and assume Eθ[(T−ψ(θ))Sθᵀ]=Dψ(θ). Then Covθ(T)⪰Dψ(θ)I(θ)⁻¹Dψ(θ)ᵀ, where A⪰B means aᵀ(A−B)a≥0 for every a∈Rᵏ.",
